id: pm-02z97f
title: "GH-1518: recover provably dead same-host item-lock owners before TTL expiry"
description: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1518 reports on published 2026.10.20/Linux/plain non-Git trackers that a killed public-SDK lock holder leaves an item unavailable for the full 3600-second TTL. Later update/comments calls and force recovery refuse after the normal wait, while health counts the receipt as active. This is reporter evidence; current-head reproduction and implementation remain pending. The new boundary is provable same-host process death before TTL expiry, rather than expired-lock GC, live-lock throughput or safe ownership publication."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: agent-ux,"area:locking",concurrency
created_at: "2026-10-20T10:34:24.727Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T17:50:03.975Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-20T17:50:02.063Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-20T17:50:02.063Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Add owned-sandbox SDK and CLI crash recovery tests. Record enough host/process-start identity to distinguish a dead original owner from PID reuse, foreign hosts, EPERM/unknown liveness and legacy receipts. Reclaim only with positive proof through the existing token-validated stale-cleanup gate, preserving initialization and single-winner takeover invariants. Keep unknown/live owners and malformed/partial receipts conservative. Health, GC and conflict recovery should consistently expose liveness/staleness and an actionable actual command; record recovery provenance without losing acknowledged writes."
parent: pm-dj98
risk: high
confidence: medium
resolution: "Record verifiable Linux owner identity and recover positively dead original owners before TTL through the existing writer gate. SDK acquisition and GC share each gated owner-death observation with its audit obligation; GC compares unchanged bytes and reports retention for all audit failures. Preserve live/unknown protection, history and expired-lease policy with explicit caller fencing guidance."
expected_result: "SDK acquisition and GC reclaim dead original owners with durable audit intent, retain unexpired live/unknown owners and replaced receipts, report audit failures truthfully, and preserve acknowledged item writes and history."
actual_result: "All116 linked tests pass. Three audit controls fail before their respective repairs and pass afterward: transient GC probe, audit ENOENT and transient SDK probe with force. Final build, complete typechecking and lint pass. Prior4c564f1d4 hosted checks pass CLEAN; final source still requires its CI and next included free full review before merge. Fresh bounded Sentry and paired telemetry verification pass."
